v7 ADDITION - new optimisation on top of the v6 rebase
=====================================================================

gcc/simplify-rtx.cc: fuse nested VEC_MERGEs that share an operand.

    (vec_merge (vec_merge A B sel0) B sel)  ->  (vec_merge A B (sel0 & sel))
    (vec_merge A (vec_merge A B sel1) sel)  ->  (vec_merge A B (sel | sel1))

Upstream already folds the two degenerate cases where one arm of the
inner merge is entirely unused (!(sel & sel0) and !(sel & ~sel0)), and
separately handles equal operands and all-zero / all-ones masks.  The
general fusion above was missing, so a sequence that touches several
lanes of a vector one lane at a time never collapsed.

Concrete effect on x86 with the insertps-zero hunk this patch already
adds to ix86_expand_vector_set (measured with the ms178 GCC 16.1.1
r581 build, -O2 -march=raptorlake):

    v4sf f(v4sf v) { v[0]=0; v[2]=0; return v; }
      before:  vinsertps $1,%xmm0,%xmm0,%xmm0
               vinsertps $4,%xmm0,%xmm0,%xmm0
      after:   vinsertps $5,%xmm0,%xmm0,%xmm0     (one insn)

    three zeroed lanes went from three insertps to one.

RTL evidence for why it was needed: combine already tried the merge and
gave up -

    Trying 7 -> 10:
        7: r101:V4SF=vec_merge(r104:V4SF,const_vector,0xe)
       10: r103:V4SF=vec_merge(r101:V4SF,const_vector,0xb)
    Failed to match this instruction

0xe & 0xb = 0xa, which is a valid operand for
sse4_1_insertps_<mode>_zero (it requires IN_RANGE (op3, 1, 14)).

CORRECTNESS
  The rewrite depends only on the masks, so it was model-checked
  exhaustively over every mask pair for N = 2, 4 and 8 lanes
  (131,616 lane-by-lane comparisons, 0 mismatches), and by random
  sampling for N = 16 (200,000 pairs, 0 mismatches).  A deliberately
  wrong variant (sel0 | sel instead of sel0 & sel) was checked to be
  rejected by the same model (240 mismatches at N = 4), confirming the
  test has discriminating power.  Both new blocks are guarded by
  rtx_equal_p on the shared operand and by !side_effects_p, matching
  the conventions of the surrounding rules, and the result is masked
  with MASK so no bits outside the lane count can escape.

  A regression test is included:
    gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/i386/ms178-vec-merge-fuse-1.c

Applies with ZERO fuzz, ZERO offsets, ZERO rejects on
bcda9a5a1d995c1a0fe1fb64bfd4dddd44224ba5 (patch -F0 and git apply
